ap as well but as the camera pans  upwards closer to link we can see what  seems to be a large floating building in  the distance  because of the clouds we can only see  the very top of it however in the very  next shot we see a similar looking  structure on the top right of the frame  which is possibly the very same building  from a different vantage point we can  also see some additional smaller  constructions on the islands right here  these in turn look like they might be of  the same type as the one from the next  shot  which is in my opinion the most  beautiful looking one in the entire  trailer we can see two things  some man-made walls and some sort of  archway which kind of reminds me of a  japanese torii gate the next scene is  where we get a first more detailed look  at one of the new buildings but we'll go  over the actual details later  next we have the shot of link flying  past a bunch of pokoblins riding a stone  talus which is amazing  by the way in the first few frames  however we can see some small details on  the left of the frame  now this building right here looks like  the ruins we are familiar with  in fact i'm pretty sure this is long  long range since we can also see a small  section of castle town right here but  these two pieces of debris right here  don't look familiar at all the shape  clearly shows that it is man-made but  these were definitely not in breath of  the wild they seem to originate from the  same type of walls we saw in the sky  which leads me to believe that these  might be pieces that have broken off  when the islands rose to the sky  and then landed in hyrule field next we  have the close-up of the green hand and  although it doesn't show an  actual building we do see that link is  laying on a piece of floor with a  circular shape to it and is decorated  with an unknown scripture  again more details later in the part  where link uses his new  stasis time manipulation thingy we can  see some new types of enemy camps they  