t i thought they were gerudo  scripture but when you pull up the  gerudo alphabet they are definitely not  the same  the only one that kinda looks like a  gerudo symbol is this one right here  which bears some resemblance to the a  or e but even this is not a complete  match whatever this language is it  probably has something to do with the  tribe that built these structures  furthermore a lot of the small buildings  we see on the various floating islands  have the same open design that is to say  a floor with pillars and a roof but no  walls  in the shot where we see one of them up  close we can also see some sort of stone  altar perhaps these will serve as this  game's variant of fast travel points  seeing as there's no trace of any of the  sheikah shrines or towers anywhere in  hyrule's landscape this could mean that  once you visit an island you can easily  travel back there in the future  the only building that sticks out from  the rest is the big one in the first two  shots we covered it still seems to have  the same grey stonework but it's much  bigger and does seem to have closed  walls  at the same time it also has the same  feature where it gets wider at the top  i'm really hoping that this might be one  of the game's dungeons who knows maybe  the shot inside that enclosed space  where link is using his new flamethrower  ability might be  inside this building now the big  questions remain who built these  structures and how did they get here  i mean they certainly weren't there in  breath the wild obviously  the zonai would be a prime candidate  once again but there is however  one issue as elusive as the zone i are  their architecture is the one thing we  do know  quite a lot about and none of the  buildings seen in the new trailer are  unmistakably of  zonai origin yes they do have some  similar features  such as the swarvey tf-like decorations  and blocky design best seen on the  sargon bridge but it's just  different enough that we can say with  certainty that these are  zone i made there's no trace of the  recognizable spiral the snake engravings  or other ornaments on some of the walls  and statues now it could be that they  decided to  alter zonai architecture for this game  plus we've only seen a few buildings in  ruins so far  maybe there are more out there that do  feature the zonai characteristics we are  familiar with  i am quite certain that this is not  ancient hylian the ruins we find of them  are much more in line with roman  building styles such as round pillars  and smooth archways this new building  style is way too blocky compared to that  and as opposed to zonai architecture  which does have some resemblances  there are no features that match with  ancient hylian i will do a more in-depth  video  about the zonai connections in a later  video as there are definitely some  besides the architecture  finally we have the question of how in  the heck did these buildings suddenly  appear in the first place  like i said they were definitely not  there in breath of the wild i don't have  any definitive answers  obviously but there are two options that  came to my mind and could explain it  best  the first and most talked about option  right now is that the parts where we see  link traversing the skies takes place in  the past  far far in the past as a matter of fact  say these buildings  are indeed of zonai origin we could be  looking at an ancient version of hyrule  which of course would mean that time  travel is back  once again and this is definitely a  possibility in fact there are quite a  few time related hints all throughout  the trailer we see time manipulation  ability specifically a theme of  reversing time  then there's the fact that link is  wearing some very old school looking  clothing in some of the shots  they kind of remind me of roman or  ancient greek with the toga that only  covers one shoulder and the open  sandals in every shot where link is in  the sky he is wearing that same green  attire on his upper body whereas on the  surface he has always seen donning the  tunic we recognize from the first  trailer  in general hyrule looks different some  like mass nintendo bandit have already  pointed out some missing buildings that  were there in the previous game but are  gone now  indicating that this might take place in  an era before these were built  so yeah this could very well be taking  place far in the past but there is a  second option  and that is that the floating islands we  see are not pieces of hyrule's surface  from breath of the wild but instead new  landmasses that have perhaps  always existed far above the clouds just  because we see  hyrule castle rising doesn't  automatically mean that the rest of  hyrule will do so as well  yes i did suggest this in my video last  week but that was just a suggestion that  doesn't mean it's true  in fact even after hours of scrutinizing  the trailer i have yet to see  anything on the floating islands that i  recognize as something i know from the  surface  we also don't see any craters on the  surface from above  at least not right now anyway and even  in terms of the castle  who's to say it will rise up as high as  the clouds in the final shot it seems to  have stopped moving and it's just  floating there maybe this is the extent  of it it will just stay there like this  surrounded by malice a bit like ganon's  castle from ocarina of time  and that about covers the architecture  for now i hope to see you in the next  episode where i will go more in depth on  other aspects of the new trailer  the next part will be released very soon  and if you have your own ideas and  findings don't shy away from sharing  them down in the comments i might even  use them in a future episode  a big big thanks to everyone for the  amazing e3 live stream to my friends  charlie and mike for being there with me  and the amazing presents i got from you  guys  and lastly thank you to my ever so  gracious patreons and members and to  arno danboof  fume kage tokoyami andrei lechchilin  michael egger and an additional shout  out to shigeyako for upgrading their  pledge you are all  amazing as always and that is  all for now this is don signing off and  it's in the sky  [Music]  you

